# addSelectedRows

`addSelectedRows` keeps track of selected items in the table. Works with sub-rows.

## Options

<Admonition type="info">Options passed into <code>addSelectedRows</code>.</Admonition>

```ts {3}
const table = createTable(data, {
  select: addSelectedRows({ ... }),
});
```

### `initialSelectedDataIds?: Record<string, boolean>`
Initial selected row data ids (by `row.dataId`). Default `{}`.

### `linkDataSubRows?: boolean`
Link parent/sub-row selection when updating. Default `true`.

## Column Options

<Admonition type="info">Options passed into column definitions.</Admonition>

```ts {7}
const columns = table.createColumns([
  table.column({
    header: 'Name',
    accessor: 'name',
    plugins: {
      select: { ... },
    },
  }),
]);
```

## Prop Set

<Admonition type="info">Extensions to the view model. Read <code>current.props</code> on table components. The lists below are generated from the plugin's TypeScript prop-set type, so they match the published package exactly.</Admonition>

<PluginProps set="SelectedRowsPropSet" pluginKey="select" />

## Interactions

- `allPageRowsSelected` and `somePageRowsSelected` are scoped to the current page from `addPagination`, not the whole data set. Use `allRowsSelected` for the entire table.
- The page-scoped values read the view model's `current.pageRows`, which is computed on demand, so they work the same in a template, a test or headless code.
- With `addSubRows`, selecting a parent selects its sub-rows, and `someSubRowsSelected` / `allSubRowsSelected` on the parent reflect the children's state.

## Plugin State

<Admonition type="info">State provided by <code>addSelectedRows</code>.</Admonition>

```ts {3}
const vm = table.createViewModel(columns)
const { pluginStates } = vm
const { selectedDataIds, allRowsSelected, getRowState } = pluginStates.select
```

### `selectedDataIds: RecordSet`
The selected data ids (`row.dataId`). Read `selectedDataIds.current` (a `Record<string, boolean>` holding only `true` entries), or change it with `add(id)`, `remove(id)`, `toggle(id)`, `addAll(ids)`, `removeAll(ids)`, `clear()` and `has(id)`.

```svelte
{Object.keys(selectedDataIds.current).length} row(s) selected.
<button onclick={() => selectedDataIds.clear()}>Clear selection</button>
```

### `allRowsSelected: Box<boolean>`
Whether every row is selected. Writing `true` selects every row; `false` clears the selection.

### `someRowsSelected: ReadonlyBox<boolean>`

### `allPageRowsSelected: Box<boolean>`
Whether every row on the current page is selected. Writing selects or deselects the page's rows.

### `somePageRowsSelected: ReadonlyBox<boolean>`

### `getRowState: (row) => SelectedRowsRowState`
Returns the selection state of a `BodyRow`:

- `isSelected: Box<boolean>`: writing selects or deselects the row (and, with `linkDataSubRows`, its sub-rows)
- `isSomeSubRowsSelected: ReadonlyBox<boolean>`
- `isAllSubRowsSelected: ReadonlyBox<boolean>`

The views hold no state of their own (they read `selectedDataIds`), so they never go stale; the same row object always returns the same views.

<Admonition type="info">v7 removed <code>invalidate()</code>: there is no per-row cache to clear.</Admonition>

A checkbox takes the boxes as props:

```svelte
<!-- SelectIndicator.svelte, rendered with createRender(SelectIndicator, getRowState(row)) -->
<script lang="ts">
    import type { Box, ReadonlyBox } from '@humanspeak/svelte-headless-table'
    const { isSelected, isSomeSubRowsSelected }: {
        isSelected: Box<boolean>
        isSomeSubRowsSelected: ReadonlyBox<boolean>
    } = $props()
</script>

<input
    type="checkbox"
    checked={isSelected.current}
    indeterminate={isSomeSubRowsSelected.current}
    onchange={(e) => (isSelected.current = e.currentTarget.checked)}
/>
```

